# Docker runtime library

- `internal/docker` (images, containers, static add-ons) and `internal/volumes` (managed volumes) shell out to the host `docker` CLI. They are legacy code kept compiling but **not wired to any HTTP route**; task C replaces them with the Docker runner behind the planned `/api/v1/servers`, `/images` and `/volumes` routes (types in `internal/apitypes/servers.go` and `host.go`).
- Do not wire these packages to HTTP as they are: they print to stdout, return raw command output in errors and do not validate inputs. Errors from Docker must reach clients only as safe messages (see the HTTP API rule).
- `GET /api/v1/status` checks Docker reachability with its own cached probe in `internal/daemon`, not with this package.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/docker/... ./internal/volumes/...` (no Docker daemon required).
